FloppyBridge driver sources: portability fixes for the GCC/MinGW libretro build.

These are applied to the pristine RobSmithDev/FloppyDriveBridge sources after they
are copied into sources/src/floppybridge/. Five unrelated problems, all of them
"upstream only ever built this with MSVC and _UNICODE":

  floppybridge_config.h    Upstream maps each ROMTYPE_ to WinUAE's ROMTYPE_FLOPYBRDGEn
                           expansion-ROM identifier, which PuAE has no equivalent of.
                           They are only ever tested with #ifdef, never used as a
                           value, so they become plain enable switches - which is
                           exactly what upstream's own windows/FloppyBridge.cpp does.

  ftdi.h                   Upstream includes <Windows.h> from *inside* namespace FTDI.
                           MSVC survives it only because windows.h is always already
                           included by the time ftdi.h is reached. Compiling ftdi.cpp
                           first with GCC drags the whole Win32 SDK - and the libstdc++
                           headers behind it - into the namespace, and cstdlib then
                           fails with "'abs' has not been declared in '::'". Pulling
                           windows.h in at global scope first makes the in-namespace
                           include a no-op via its own guard.

  ftdi.cpp                 LoadLibrary(L"FTD2XX.DLL") - a wide literal handed to the
  GreaseWeazleBridge.cpp   TCHAR-mapped macro, which is the -A variant here because
  ArduinoFloppyBridge.cpp  this build is not _UNICODE. Same for six RegQueryValueEx /
                           RegSetValueEx calls, which upstream already sits next to its
                           own RegCreateKeyExA. Switched to the explicit -A variants
                           with narrow literals; the registry values are unchanged.
                           The same three RegSetValueEx calls also pass NULL for the
                           3rd parameter, which is 'DWORD Reserved' and not a pointer -
                           harmless under MSVC, where NULL is plain 0, but GCC's __null
                           trips -Wconversion-null. Passed as 0.

  SerialIO.cpp             SetupDiGetDeviceProperty has no TCHAR mapping macro in
                           MinGW's SetupAPI.h. The buffer is WCHAR[128], so the -W
                           variant is what MSVC resolved it to anyway.

Do NOT define UNICODE/_UNICODE to fix these instead: floppybridge_lib.h's TCharString
fields are shared with disk.c, which is compiled without it, so TCHAR must stay char
across every translation unit.

Pinned to FloppyDriveBridge @ 710fa15 (v1.6.0.5). See docs/floppy.md section 3c.

